# Third-party pieces of the Windows app's server payload (Epic 38, story 38.11), x86_64.
# Every download is checked against the SHA-256 here before it is used; bumping a piece
# is a reviewed change to this file. Sourced by payload.sh (KEY=VALUE only).
# Sources, licences and why each was chosen: README.md in this directory.

# PostgreSQL 16 (the repo's major: compose, CI), theseus-rs/postgresql-binaries: the EDB
# Windows build, repackaged (relocatable, OpenSSL and ICU beside the programs, the contrib
# extensions Maktaba uses: pg_trgm, pgcrypto, unaccent). pgbin (Epic 37, feat/node-replica)
# pins this same archive for windows/amd64; once pgbin is on main, a test there keeps the
# two equal (as TestPinsMatchTheMacApp does for the Mac's).
POSTGRES_VERSION=16.15.0
POSTGRES_URL=https://github.com/theseus-rs/postgresql-binaries/releases/download/16.15.0/postgresql-16.15.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip
POSTGRES_SHA256=98fe43cff00f5aef4a7669adb575655e913dc65b1fdfb997c46fe3c1e07f4efb

# pgvector 0.8.7 (semantic search in Postgres, specs/epics/43-pgvector-search), the source
# tag the Mac's and Linux's payloads build too: payload.sh builds it with Visual C++
# (Makefile.win, nmake, PGROOT = the PostgreSQL above, no /arch) into postgres\lib and
# postgres\share\extension. PostgreSQL License.
PGVECTOR_VERSION=0.8.7
PGVECTOR_URL=https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector/archive/refs/tags/v0.8.7.tar.gz
PGVECTOR_SHA256=cac0b10c360f05b2d521200105ba3697e773d4cd3731f5a915a7e37ebe0bea85

# ffmpeg / ffprobe 8.1.2 (the Mac's release), static, from gyan.dev's GitHub mirror
# (GyanD/codexffmpeg). The "essentials" build has what Maktaba's TV runs on Windows:
# h264_nvenc and -hwaccel cuda (scale_cuda), libx264, loudnorm, subtitles; the "full"
# build only adds codecs Maktaba does not use (its zip is 266 MB, not 110). GPLv3
# (--enable-gpl --enable-version3).
FFMPEG_VERSION=8.1.2
FFMPEG_URL=https://github.com/GyanD/codexffmpeg/releases/download/8.1.2/ffmpeg-8.1.2-essentials_build.zip
FFMPEG_SHA256=db580001caa24ac104c8cb856cd113a87b0a443f7bdf47d8c12b1d740584a2ec

# CPython 3.12 (pipeline/.python-version), astral-sh/python-build-standalone,
# install_only_stripped: relocatable, OpenSSL built in. The Mac's release.
PYTHON_VERSION=3.12.15
PYTHON_URL=https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases/download/20261003/cpython-3.12.15%2B20261003-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-install_only_stripped.tar.gz
PYTHON_SHA256=6fba7f2ae506facf41d457ea8293c7497910a675c69a4e954875169410a50402

# The Visual C++ runtime beside postgres.exe (vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll,
# msvcp140.dll): not a download but Visual Studio's own redistributable folder, so the build
# machine must hold this release, checked by each DLL's FileVersion (all three carry it) and
# its Microsoft signature. Visual Studio 2026's (VC\Redist\MSVC\14.51.36231), which
# windows-latest carries (windows-2025-vs2026 image 20261018.275.1). payload.sh looks through
# every redistributable folder of every Visual Studio installed for it. When the runner's
# Visual Studio moves on, the build stops and names the version it found: bumping this line
# is a reviewed change (README.md, "The Visual C++ runtime").
MSVC_RUNTIME_VERSION=14.51.36247.0
